1
00:00:03,520 --> 00:00:04,350
The End

2
00:00:04,880 --> 00:00:05,710
Sanctuary!

3
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:09,240
Goddammit, I ain't got all day!

4
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:11,230
Huh?

5
00:00:19,960 --> 00:00:24,620
Like I thought, there's not a trace
of mold on you, even though you fell.

6
00:00:25,380 --> 00:00:30,145
I thought Chocolatous green tea was supposed
to ravage any living thing in touch.

7
00:00:30,760 --> 00:00:33,289
So how the hell are
you still in one piece?

8
00:00:34,580 --> 00:00:37,639
Guess I'll just have to do
it the old-fashioned way.

9
00:00:37,760 --> 00:00:41,860
Beating you over and over again
until your body stops moving.

10
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:46,280
Welcome to my sanctuary!

11
00:00:51,480 --> 00:00:53,240
This won't be a quick kill.

12
00:00:53,700 --> 00:00:55,957
I need to put some
distance between us fast.

13
00:00:56,040 --> 00:00:57,420
No time to lose.

14
00:00:59,940 --> 00:01:02,200
Oh, my God.

15
00:01:03,820 --> 00:01:08,780
Cameo no sa tame ni sa e?

16
00:01:09,900 --> 00:01:14,160
Hang o Hear Cairo su.

17
00:01:14,780 --> 00:01:15,860
GameStop.

18
00:01:39,580 --> 00:01:42,380
Let's go.

19
00:02:44,200 --> 00:02:47,280
That malicious mole should
be far behind by now.

20
00:03:03,180 --> 00:03:05,280
What the hell's going on?

21
00:03:05,380 --> 00:03:07,137
What's with all these accidents?

22
00:03:07,220 --> 00:03:08,050
Help me!

23
00:03:08,133 --> 00:03:08,963
An ambulance!

24
00:03:09,046 --> 00:03:09,876
Over there!

25
00:03:09,959 --> 00:03:10,789
Down by the stairs!

26
00:03:12,140 --> 00:03:13,880
Where did all the mold go?

27
00:03:15,240 --> 00:03:16,070
Chocohata!

28
00:03:16,260 --> 00:03:17,660
No one's getting eaten.

29
00:03:18,140 --> 00:03:19,860
That means they did it.

30
00:03:20,220 --> 00:03:22,420
Well done, Ragazzi. Excellent work.

31
00:03:24,660 --> 00:03:26,180
Squalo, it's me.

32
00:03:26,860 --> 00:03:28,137
Have you disposed of Buchorati?

33
00:03:28,220 --> 00:03:32,200
See, I've run into a few
complications on my end.

34
00:03:32,540 --> 00:03:34,500
I get around to killing Giorno,

35
00:03:34,700 --> 00:03:37,818
but I've taken a bit of a
hindering blow to the head.

36
00:03:38,940 --> 00:03:43,000
So to err on the side of caution,
I must share something with you.

37
00:03:43,500 --> 00:03:44,735
Listen closely, Seko.

38
00:03:45,120 --> 00:03:47,820
Those bastards are
headed for the Coliseum.

39
00:03:48,020 --> 00:03:50,820
The Bone Boys babbling bullets said so.

40
00:03:51,820 --> 00:03:54,114
They're supposed to meet someone there.

41
00:03:54,660 --> 00:03:59,072
Someone who boasts of having secret
knowledge on how to fake with the boss.

42
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:02,037
It should baffle no one
then that Giorno and his

43
00:04:02,120 --> 00:04:05,397
friends would be so eager to
make it to this rendezvous.

44
00:04:05,480 --> 00:04:07,300
Are you getting any of this?

45
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:10,440
You must uncover this
secret before anyone else.

46
00:04:11,140 --> 00:04:12,640
I'm counting on you.

47
00:04:20,580 --> 00:04:22,760
All that drama over a phone call.

48
00:04:23,300 --> 00:04:24,771
Still, what did he learn?

49
00:04:26,080 --> 00:04:27,780
Screw you, Cioccolata!

50
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:30,740
You thought I'd get all weepy over you?

51
00:04:30,920 --> 00:04:32,273
Give me a break, loser!

52
00:04:32,640 --> 00:04:34,440
You lost to clowns!

53
00:04:36,100 --> 00:04:38,797
Aren't you supposed to
be some kind of genius?

54
00:04:38,880 --> 00:04:43,704
With perfect throwing arms full of yummy
sugar cubes and a crazy fat load of cash?

55
00:04:44,080 --> 00:04:46,280
On top of that, you're super strong.

56
00:04:46,900 --> 00:04:48,547
At least I thought you were.

57
00:04:49,280 --> 00:04:54,200
It's the only reason why I've been
bothering to listen to you this entire time.

58
00:04:56,300 --> 00:04:59,120
But it turns out you're
just another weakling!

59
00:04:59,940 --> 00:05:02,360
You totally ate shit out there.

60
00:05:03,200 --> 00:05:08,740
Well guess what I don't want to hang
out with you anymore, so kiss my ass.

61
00:05:10,100 --> 00:05:12,977
What the he's heading
straight toward the Coliseum

62
00:05:13,060 --> 00:05:16,780
someone's clued him into our
goal after the secret, are you?

63
00:05:17,780 --> 00:05:19,140
I think not!

64
00:05:22,900 --> 00:05:24,200
Where's the other?

65
00:05:24,980 --> 00:05:26,800
Zippermen, go for the kill!

66
00:05:32,260 --> 00:05:33,090
How's this?

67
00:05:37,620 --> 00:05:38,450
Hey,

68
00:05:38,533 --> 00:05:40,957
don't you think it's funny
how the word coliseum

69
00:05:41,040 --> 00:05:43,980
sounds a hell of a lot
like the word mausoleum?

70
00:05:45,120 --> 00:05:46,557
What do you think, Mr.

71
00:05:46,640 --> 00:05:47,581
Language Expert?

72
00:05:47,760 --> 00:05:51,878
I'm sure you wouldn't mind if I sent
you there instead, now would you?

73
00:05:53,260 --> 00:05:54,090
Merda.

74
00:05:54,173 --> 00:05:57,417
I was wrong to assume the only
danger was the man in the helicopter.

75
00:05:57,500 --> 00:06:00,500
We're still miles away from
being out of the woods.

76
00:06:01,120 --> 00:06:04,473
This tunneling fiend is a
colossal threat all on his own.

77
00:06:04,780 --> 00:06:08,486
If he should slip from my grasp
and get to the Colosseum first,

78
00:06:09,420 --> 00:06:11,185
I'll have unleashed a monster!

79
00:06:16,480 --> 00:06:20,060
You're an awful pest, you
know that, Bucciarati.

80
00:06:20,380 --> 00:06:22,680
Why bother fighting back at this point?

81
00:06:23,020 --> 00:06:26,860
At such a close range, I can
outrun and outmuscle you!

82
00:06:27,340 --> 00:06:29,840
I'll swat you like a fly, little twerp!

83
00:06:38,100 --> 00:06:41,080
You're a pretty quick
thinker now, ain't ya?

84
00:06:41,800 --> 00:06:44,000
Your big brain saved you again.

85
00:06:44,300 --> 00:06:46,700
Just barely, though, so don't get cocky.

86
00:06:47,540 --> 00:06:50,180
Again, that body of yours is really weird.

87
00:06:50,620 --> 00:06:52,900
Just what the hell is wrong with you?

88
00:06:53,400 --> 00:06:57,106
You're riddled with glass, and
yet there's not a drop of blood.

89
00:06:59,940 --> 00:07:02,680
Did you see what I just saw, too?

90
00:07:03,520 --> 00:07:04,350
Weird.

91
00:07:04,440 --> 00:07:05,852
What do you think it is?

92
00:07:06,320 --> 00:07:08,757
It was somewhere on the
second level, right?

93
00:07:08,840 --> 00:07:10,520
The blinky, shiny thing?

94
00:07:11,220 --> 00:07:12,940
It happened earlier, too.

95
00:07:21,120 --> 00:07:25,080
There was something crawling in
the shadows just now. Must be shy.

96
00:07:26,080 --> 00:07:27,180
I saw it.

97
00:07:27,380 --> 00:07:29,020
It was quick, but I saw it.

98
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:30,197
It was a reflection.

99
00:07:30,280 --> 00:07:32,757
No doubt from a peeping
pair of binoculars.

100
00:07:32,840 --> 00:07:36,697
So that's the fellow you and your stupid
friends have been so desperate to meet.

101
00:07:36,780 --> 00:07:38,780
I think I saw him in a wheelchair.

102
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:40,997
One of his legs looked like a prosthetic.

103
00:07:41,080 --> 00:07:43,609
He doesn't seem like
a guy who could fight.

104
00:07:44,400 --> 00:07:46,780
Guess that secret's as good as mine now.

105
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:49,824
So you can suck him, you
bloodless sack of crap.

106
00:07:50,020 --> 00:07:52,320
Suck on these knuckles specifically!

107
00:07:57,340 --> 00:07:59,200
So now you're making fun of me.

108
00:07:59,360 --> 00:08:00,937
You and your stupid zippers.

109
00:08:01,020 --> 00:08:02,220
Eat shit, copycat.

110
00:08:02,420 --> 00:08:06,437
I'm not sure if you've forgotten, but
you're swimming around in my territory now.

111
00:08:06,520 --> 00:08:10,560
I'm gonna rip your dumbass
apart. Take this! Thank you!

112
00:08:12,460 --> 00:08:14,440
Wait, he's not hiding down there.

113
00:08:14,660 --> 00:08:16,189
He's trying to move about.

114
00:08:17,440 --> 00:08:19,980
I'm getting some crazy vibrations.

115
00:08:20,400 --> 00:08:23,871
Just where are you off to in
such a hurry, you damn coward?

116
00:08:25,320 --> 00:08:27,517
Running away with my trick? Boy,

117
00:08:27,600 --> 00:08:32,137
you got a whole lot of nerve trying to
mimic me like I'm some kind of idiotic joke.

118
00:08:32,220 --> 00:08:35,057
Bet you think you're hot shit
with your zipper stand right now.

119
00:08:35,140 --> 00:08:35,970
Well, you're not.

120
00:08:36,053 --> 00:08:38,917
All you really did was
steal my moves, little rat.

121
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:44,757
That lack of creativity is about to bite
you because I am a million times better

122
00:08:44,840 --> 00:08:49,877
at this than your dumbass will ever be you
won't send one foot in the Coliseum. The

123
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:56,960
walls

124
00:09:00,900 --> 00:09:01,730
are turning

125
00:09:01,813 --> 00:09:03,037
rubbery again so

126
00:09:03,120 --> 00:09:05,960
he's already on my trail but this noise?

127
00:09:06,720 --> 00:09:11,157
There's no question it's rushing straight
toward me with an incredible speed.

128
00:09:11,240 --> 00:09:13,977
Sound may be able to travel
fastest through solids,

129
00:09:14,060 --> 00:09:17,637
but this liquid-like material
won't offer me much protection.

130
00:09:17,720 --> 00:09:18,550
Damn it!

131
00:09:18,760 --> 00:09:22,797
That probably means he's been able to
hear my every move this whole time.

132
00:09:22,880 --> 00:09:24,586
Well, would you look at that?

133
00:09:24,740 --> 00:09:28,152
You actually got quite far for
a complete rookie, that is.

134
00:09:28,500 --> 00:09:29,740
You can't hide.

135
00:09:29,900 --> 00:09:31,537
I know exactly where you are.

136
00:09:31,620 --> 00:09:34,880
A pathetic 20 meters ahead
and slightly to the left.

137
00:09:36,820 --> 00:09:38,040
Turning right, huh?

138
00:09:38,360 --> 00:09:39,654
Ten more meters to go.

139
00:09:40,660 --> 00:09:42,440
Now just seven meters.

140
00:09:42,720 --> 00:09:43,920
Five meters.

141
00:09:44,980 --> 00:09:47,333
Strangling you now would be too lenient.

142
00:09:47,620 --> 00:09:51,820
Hope you know you've just buried
yourself alive, Bucciarati.

143
00:09:52,140 --> 00:09:55,375
How are you gonna dodge when
you're surrounded by dirt?

144
00:09:55,640 --> 00:09:59,699
It'll be no different from punching
a helplessly tied up little worm.

145
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:01,500
Just two more meters.

146
00:10:04,740 --> 00:10:05,920
A water pipe.

147
00:10:07,180 --> 00:10:09,720
You're trying to shake
me with that? Idiot.

148
00:10:10,420 --> 00:10:12,460
What the hell do you take me for?

149
00:10:14,660 --> 00:10:16,460
You out of smart ideas?

150
00:10:16,960 --> 00:10:21,489
Oh, these pathetic little stunts of
yours freaking reek of utter desperation.

151
00:10:21,660 --> 00:10:23,777
You don't even have to say a single word.

152
00:10:23,860 --> 00:10:25,057
Judging from your actions,

153
00:10:25,140 --> 00:10:27,057
I can already tell
you've come to terms with

154
00:10:27,140 --> 00:10:29,177
meeting your end at the
hands of my sanctuary.

155
00:10:29,260 --> 00:10:31,420
I'm not sure exactly where,

156
00:10:31,600 --> 00:10:35,188
but I can sense your carcass
languishing just 20 meters away.

157
00:10:36,260 --> 00:10:38,917
Staying still in the hopes
that I won't find you, huh?

158
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:40,500
Just like a little bunny.

159
00:10:41,200 --> 00:10:42,820
Or are you up to something?

160
00:10:43,120 --> 00:10:44,360
Let me guess.

161
00:10:44,820 --> 00:10:46,220
You got another plan?

162
00:10:46,500 --> 00:10:48,441
You're a quick thinker after all.

163
00:10:49,340 --> 00:10:50,280
Too bad.

164
00:10:53,340 --> 00:10:56,817
All the brains in the world
can't save you from me now.

165
00:10:56,900 --> 00:10:59,540
Time for you to die, Smarty Pants!

166
00:11:04,360 --> 00:11:06,180
That sound just now is new.

167
00:11:06,660 --> 00:11:07,800
What's he up to?

168
00:11:08,580 --> 00:11:10,540
It's got me surrounded. Damn.

169
00:11:21,540 --> 00:11:25,060
Even all those big rocks in the ground...

170
00:11:25,800 --> 00:11:29,624
turn right into mud when they're
exposed to my Sanctuary's touch.

171
00:11:32,800 --> 00:11:36,080
But the moment my body
starts moving away from them,

172
00:11:36,360 --> 00:11:38,820
they harden right back into stone.

173
00:11:43,980 --> 00:11:45,880
Got a little tip for you.

174
00:11:46,200 --> 00:11:49,937
Listen well and you'll definitely
make it out of this alive, maybe.

175
00:11:50,020 --> 00:11:54,580
The only thing you gotta do to live is
remain as still as you possibly can.

176
00:11:59,560 --> 00:12:03,137
I mean, I guess it'd take a real
miracle for you to pull that off.

177
00:12:03,220 --> 00:12:05,837
Like you must have heard of the
guy who was hanged three times,

178
00:12:05,920 --> 00:12:08,877
but lived because the rope kept
breaking every time they dropped him.

179
00:12:08,960 --> 00:12:09,901
Ain't that nuts?

180
00:12:10,480 --> 00:12:13,245
Miss Zero, I can't stay
down here much longer.

181
00:12:14,480 --> 00:12:17,009
But resurfacing now
isn't an option either.

182
00:12:20,260 --> 00:12:22,217
I prepared myself for this.

183
00:12:22,300 --> 00:12:27,120
But should they fail to make it, I'll
have no choice but to destroy the Arrow.

184
00:12:27,800 --> 00:12:31,380
All hope hinges on them
crossing paths with it.

185
00:12:32,420 --> 00:12:37,600
If, in his true heart of hearts, a
hero wishes to defeat Emperor Crimson,

186
00:12:37,900 --> 00:12:41,253
he will have no choice but to
learn of the Arrow's power.

187
00:12:41,980 --> 00:12:46,200
Fate has decided that hero
shall not be me, but them.

188
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:51,760
Twelve years ago, it entered my
possession after the battle in Egypt.

189
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:56,977
The horrors this artifact has wrought will

190
00:12:57,060 --> 00:13:00,140
continue to rage on until they stop it.

191
00:13:09,780 --> 00:13:13,060
It's all rather ironic,
one might venture to say.

192
00:13:13,460 --> 00:13:17,620
Deemed pariahs and cast from society,
they sought family in the Mafia.

193
00:13:18,360 --> 00:13:22,757
Yet here they are, determined to save the
same world from which they were shunned.

194
00:13:22,840 --> 00:13:26,320
I can do little more than
hope that you, Bucciarati,

195
00:13:26,740 --> 00:13:28,799
will be able to make it here alive.

196
00:13:28,900 --> 00:13:32,076
All will be rendered pointless
if you fail to triumph.

197
00:13:32,340 --> 00:13:37,060
When that happens, the arrow and
its secret must fade into oblivion.

198
00:13:37,580 --> 00:13:40,940
So I patiently await
you, Harbinger of Hope.

199
00:13:41,200 --> 00:13:43,820
It's the only thing I'm able to do.

200
00:13:44,540 --> 00:13:46,320
We'll begin once you're here.

201
00:13:47,200 --> 00:13:50,320
Until then, I'll continue
to preserve its true power.

202
00:13:50,940 --> 00:13:55,220
Just as I have been for all those
interminable and torturous years.

203
00:13:59,500 --> 00:14:01,540
It's no use. I gotta move.

204
00:14:03,240 --> 00:14:04,400
There he goes.

205
00:14:04,680 --> 00:14:06,160
He finally gave in.

206
00:14:06,920 --> 00:14:10,420
Is that you I hear squirming
around 12 meters to the right?

207
00:14:10,740 --> 00:14:14,297
Wait, you can't be thinking about
taking shelter under the Coliseum.

208
00:14:14,380 --> 00:14:16,817
That's the dumbest idea you've had today?

209
00:14:16,900 --> 00:14:19,580
As if I let you do that!

210
00:14:23,860 --> 00:14:25,177
He's coming in hot!

211
00:14:25,260 --> 00:14:29,180
I can hear him frantically
working his way closer and closer!

212
00:14:31,460 --> 00:14:33,057
Such a noisy target!

213
00:14:33,140 --> 00:14:37,257
I can easily tell he's just ten meters
in front of me now eight meters!

214
00:14:37,340 --> 00:14:40,177
I can't possibly hope to outrun him!

215
00:14:40,260 --> 00:14:41,160
Come forth!

216
00:14:56,820 --> 00:14:58,117
Whoa! Not bad.

217
00:14:58,200 --> 00:14:59,600
I take it back.

218
00:14:59,740 --> 00:15:01,916
This was a damn cool scheme for sure.

219
00:15:03,360 --> 00:15:04,560
Oh, Bucciarati,

220
00:15:04,820 --> 00:15:09,337
is this really how the great mafioso
flails when he's been backed into a corner?

221
00:15:09,420 --> 00:15:10,250
Well,

222
00:15:10,333 --> 00:15:15,580
big congrats to you on being the first
person to successfully hide from Sanctuary,

223
00:15:15,780 --> 00:15:17,545
even if it was just for a bit.

224
00:15:18,540 --> 00:15:20,060
But playtime's over.

225
00:15:20,300 --> 00:15:22,120
I'll get you any second now.

226
00:15:22,300 --> 00:15:23,653
You can't hide forever.

227
00:15:23,780 --> 00:15:26,357
Of course, you're welcome
to try if you want.

228
00:15:26,440 --> 00:15:29,200
It'll just make killing
you that much sweeter.

229
00:15:32,640 --> 00:15:33,757
What happened?

230
00:15:33,840 --> 00:15:35,180
My skin, it's...

231
00:15:40,580 --> 00:15:43,500
Even the stone pavement
is melting into mud!

232
00:15:43,700 --> 00:15:46,560
And so will your body
once I finally get to it!

233
00:15:46,780 --> 00:15:49,860
The closer I get, the Capri you'll become!

234
00:15:50,180 --> 00:15:51,474
Isn't that just swell?

235
00:15:52,260 --> 00:15:54,180
Found you! You're mine!

236
00:16:02,600 --> 00:16:06,300
You really made me work for
it, but I've got you at last!

237
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:10,140
All that remains between us
is one and a half meters.

238
00:16:14,100 --> 00:16:17,480
Look how close you got to
making it to the Coliseum.

239
00:16:18,060 --> 00:16:20,640
Gosh darn it, you almost got there.

240
00:16:21,100 --> 00:16:22,300
Well, too bad!

241
00:16:22,500 --> 00:16:24,618
That tantalizing secret is all mine!

242
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:26,380
Zipperman, showtime!

243
00:16:28,360 --> 00:16:29,190
Huh?

244
00:16:29,640 --> 00:16:31,758
Some people might call it a miracle.

245
00:16:32,320 --> 00:16:33,400
Even I'm baffled.

246
00:16:34,160 --> 00:16:38,219
I could shatter any bone in my body
without feeling an ounce of pain.

247
00:16:38,440 --> 00:16:41,499
My heart doesn't beat, so
I don't bleed much either.

248
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:43,840
Nothing truly hurts me anymore.

249
00:16:44,600 --> 00:16:46,980
Knowing that, I laid a trap for you.

250
